  "caption": "Quinn googled a sore hip, read \"bursitis\" and the panic was instant. Hip sore at night, legs crossed at the desk all day… sound familiar?\n\nA bursa is a small fluid-filled cushion that helps tendons glide. In the hip and shoulder the tendon is often the bigger part of the picture.\n\nWhat may help: ease the squeeze (uncross your legs, avoid sleeping on the sore side), build tendon strength gradually instead of only resting, keep weekly activity steady, and use padding if you kneel a lot.\n\nA hot, red, swollen area with fever needs same-day medical care. Pain that lingers or worsens is worth getting assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
